              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Increase support if needed"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Escalate if the patient deteriorates or fails to improve."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "venturi_mask_group_21",
              "group_title": "Commonly taught Venturi adapter colours",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The following are examples of a commonly encountered colour scheme, not a universal standard. Always confirm the printed FiO₂ and flow instructions on the actual device."
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Adapter colour",
                    "Commonly associated FiO₂"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Blue",
                      "24%"
                    ],
                    [
                      "White",
                      "28%"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Orange",
                      "31%"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Yellow",
                      "35%"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Red",
                      "40%"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Green",
                      "60% on some systems"
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Memory aid: Blue 24, white 28 — then remember that intermediate and higher concentrations vary with the manufacturer's adapter set."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "venturi_mask_subsection_13",
          "subsection_title": ". Mnemonic for Color Order",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "venturi_mask_group_22",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "To remember the order of colors from \"Blue Whales Yawn Red Gills\""
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "venturi_mask_subsection_14",
          "subsection_title": "Alternative Story Mnemonic",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "venturi_mask_group_23",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "If visual stories work better for you:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "\"The BLUE sky (24%) turned WHITE with clouds (28%), then an ORANGE sun (31%) shone YELLOW (35%), turning RED hot (40%), until the GREEN grass grew (60%).\""
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Do not use colour alone to select an adapter in clinical practice."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "venturi_mask_subsection_15",
          "subsection_title": "Common OSCE questions and model answers",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "venturi_mask_group_24",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q1. What is the principle of a Venturi mask?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A high-velocity oxygen jet entrains room air through calibrated openings, producing an oxygen–air mixture with a specified concentration."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q2. Why is it called a fixed-performance device?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "When correctly assembled and operated at the specified flow, it delivers a relatively predictable FiO₂ compared with conventional low-flow devices."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q3. Why is it useful in COPD?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It allows controlled oxygen delivery to an appropriate target saturation in patients at risk of hypercapnic respiratory failure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q4. Why must the air-entrainment ports remain open?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "They allow the prescribed amount of room air to mix with oxygen. Obstruction can alter the delivered concentration and compromise performance."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q5. What determines the correct oxygen flow rate?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The manufacturer's instructions for the selected adapter and the patient's clinical requirements."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q6. What is the difference between a Venturi mask and a simple face mask?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The Venturi mask uses calibrated air entrainment to deliver a more predictable FiO₂. The simple face mask delivers a variable concentration."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q7. What would you do if SpO₂ remains below target?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Reassess airway, breathing, circulation, the oxygen source, flow, adapter, and ports. Escalate oxygen delivery and respiratory support as required."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q8. What is the usual initial target saturation for a patient with COPD at risk of hypercapnia?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Usually 88–92% pending blood gas results, unless a different individualised target is indicated."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q9. Does a Venturi mask provide ventilatory support?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "No. It delivers oxygen but does not provide the ventilatory assistance of non-invasive ventilation or invasive mechanical ventilation."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q10. Why is blood gas analysis important in suspected hypercapnic respiratory failure?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It measures PaCO₂ and pH, helping identify CO₂ retention and respiratory acidosis that may require ventilatory support."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "venturi_mask_subsection_16",
          "subsection_title": "Common mistakes and examiner tips",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "venturi_mask_group_25",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Mistake: Selecting an adapter by colour alone"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Check the printed oxygen concentration and flow instructions."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Mistake: Covering the entrainment ports"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Keep the ports clear of bedding, clothing, and obstruction."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Mistake: Using an arbitrary driving flow"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Set the flow specified for the chosen adapter."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Mistake: Assuming controlled FiO₂ guarantees adequate oxygenation"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Assess the patient and escalate if oxygenation or ventilation remains inadequate."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "What impresses the examiner"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Explain air entrainment, identify the adapter, specify the labelled flow, keep ports unobstructed, and explain its role in controlled oxygen therapy."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}